<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tartus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tortosa, Antaradus, Tortosa (Syria)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tartu">Tartus</a> is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, facing the island of Arwad. As Antaradus it was a mainland settlement of Arwad in antiquity, and as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tortosa">Tortosa</a> it was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader</a> stronghold held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Knights Templar</a>, whose cathedral of Our Lady survives. It is now Syria's second port.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tartus.jpg" alt="Tartus" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Taras Kalapun: xslim (Flickr) · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boats_on_Tartus_boat_harbor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Ramon Berenguer I extended Barcelona’s authority in the eleventh century, and Ramon Berenguer IV conquered <b>Tortosa</b> in 1148 and Lleida in 1149, completing what became known as New Catalonia.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Principality of Catalonia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The young commune also fought for the western Mediterranean, joining Alfonso VII of Castile against Almería and Ramon Berenguer IV of Barcelona against <b>Tortosa</b> in 1146–1148.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-genoa">Republic of Genoa · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Arwad occupies a small island off <b>Tartus</b>, giving it a sheltered harbour and natural defences.</blockquote><a href="/state/arwad">Arwad</a></li><li><blockquote>The county ran along the coast from Jubail to <b>Tortosa</b> and inland to the Orontes.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-tripoli">County of Tripoli</a></li></ul></section>
